  "id": "COMPOUND:27348 - PROTEIN:5999",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Helilandin B may interact with Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein through a series of molecular pathways. The drug, Helilandin B, is identified as a target of two distinct compounds, both of which are structural isomers of a complex azulenoid compound. These compounds are ultimately targeted by Hemiasterlin and Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit, which in turn are linked to the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. The final scores from the three paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different molecular intermediates. The evidence suggests that Helilandin B may exert its biological effects through a cascade involving these targets, potentially modulating macrophage function via the expression of the gene in question. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple pathways converging on the final target, indicating a possible regulatory or signaling role in macrophage activity.",
